# Pepper Pro configuration.
#
# Copy to `apps/pepper-pro/server/.env` and edit — that file is gitignored.
# Every value is commented out and shows the built-in default. The shared
# settings (DATA_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR, PORT, PEPPER_API_TOKEN, HF_TOKEN,
# CIVITAI_TOKEN for LoRAs from Civitai, job concurrency, retention) are the
# same as Pepper's: see apps/pepper/server/.env.example.

# --- Hardware and licences ---------------------------------------------------

# Which file variants recipes install and which recipes are offered:
# 24gb-64ram | 32gb | 48gb | 96gb. The RunPod launcher sets it with --tier.
#PEPPER_TIER=32gb

# personal | commercial. Commercial refuses recipes whose weights forbid
# commercial use (Qwen-Image's research licence). A project can also be
# marked commercial on its own.
#LICENCE_MODE=personal

# --- ComfyUI -----------------------------------------------------------------

# A ComfyUI checkout at the pinned version and its Python; the image has
# both. For a local one: scripts/install-comfy.sh (TORCH_INDEX=
# https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu for a CPU-only machine).
#COMFY_DIR=./data/comfy/ComfyUI
# Defaults to the venv install-comfy.sh makes next to COMFY_DIR, else python3.
#COMFY_PYTHON=
#COMFY_PORT=8188

# Extra custom node packs to allow, beyond those the recipes pin.
#COMFY_NODES=

# Restart ComfyUI after this many jobs, which returns memory that long
# sessions leak. 0 never restarts.
#COMFY_RECYCLE_JOBS=40

# Keep a recipe's models loaded between jobs of the same family (fast
# auditioning); off, ComfyUI is told to free them after every job.
#COMFY_KEEP_WARM=true

# Ceiling on one ComfyUI job, in ms. Video finishing runs long.
#COMFY_TIMEOUT=3600000

# --- llama.cpp ---------------------------------------------------------------

#LLAMACPP_PORT=8090
#LLAMACPP_TIMEOUT=300000
#LLAMACPP_RELEASE_REPO=searpro/llama.cpp

# The model Claude Code runs on when pointed at this server (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL;
# deploy/home/llm/claude-box.sh does it): a GGUF in DATA_DIR/models/llm, served
# at /v1/messages. Its mmproj-* file, if one matches the name, is loaded too.
# Requests wait while renders run or are queued, and a render waits only for
# the turn in progress (docs/PEPPER-PRO.md §14). Empty: the endpoint is off.
#LLM_AGENT_MODEL=Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf
# llama.cpp flags for it in long form, over the defaults (98k context, q8 cache,
# 4096 batches, one slot); sampling belongs here.
#LLM_AGENT_ARGS=--temp 0.6 --top-k 20 --top-p 0.95
# The other two models worth a session on the 16 GB box, at the 64k context
# they were measured with (start claude-box.sh with AGENT_CTX=65536 to match).
# Gemma 4 is the fastest (2,800 t/s prompt, ~75 t/s out) and needs no fixes.
#LLM_AGENT_MODEL=gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf
#LLM_AGENT_ARGS=--ctx-size 65536 --temp 1.0 --top-k 64 --top-p 0.95
# Qwen3.8 27B is dense, so a third the speed. Its own chat template rejects
# Claude Code's mid-conversation system message; the fixed one beside it
# renders that as an ordinary system turn.
#LLM_AGENT_MODEL=Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ3_S.gguf
#LLM_AGENT_ARGS=--ctx-size 65536 --temp 0.6 --top-k 20 --top-p 0.95 --chat-template-file /data/models/llm/Qwen3.8-27B-fixed.jinja

# The vision model that checks takes (analyze task `check`), by the name
# GET /v1/llm/models lists it under: a GGUF with its mmproj in DATA_DIR/models/llm.
#CHECK_MODEL=

# The model that breaks a script into scenes and shots when a project is
# started from one in the web app (Claude plans through plan_project instead).
# Defaults to CHECK_MODEL; any llama.cpp chat model works.
#PLAN_MODEL=

# --- Recipes and golden shots -------------------------------------------------

# Defaults are the recipes and shot list shipped next to the server.
#RECIPES_DIR=
#GOLDEN_FILE=
